    "title": "Netflix To Live Stream Artemis II Lunar Flyby, Global Release Time Revealed",
    "text": "Netflix will be livestreaming the Artemis II lunar flyby, having missed out on streaming the launch. The ten-day crewed mission to the moon began on April 1, 2026, with the Space Launch System (SLS) lifting off from Kennedy Space Center.Artemis II lunar flyby to live stream on NetflixNetflix is set to live-stream the Artemis II lunar flyby on April 6, 2026, at 12:00 GMT-5. The following time zones will help you determine when to tune in to the platform for the stream (via What’s on Netflix). Note that some countries may not be able to view it on the same day:North America: 10:00 a.m. Pacific Time (PT)/11:00 a.m. Mountain Time (MT)/12:00 p.m. Central Time (CT)/1:00 p.m. Eastern Time (ET)South America: 2:00 p.m. Brazilian Time (BRT)United Kingdom and Europe: 5:00 p.m. Coordinated Universal Time (UTC)/6:00 p.m. British Summer Time (BST)/7:00 p.m. Central European Time (CEST)Middle East and India: 9:00 p.m. Gulf Standard Time (GST)/10:30 p.m. Indian Standard Time (IST)Japan: 2:00 a.m. Japanese Standard Time (JST) (April 7, 2026)Australia: 3:00 a.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST) (April 7, 2026)New Zealand: 5:00 a.m. New Zealand Standard Time (NZST) (April 7, 2026)Artemis II marks the first crewed mission of the Orion spacecraft and the first to take place in low Earth orbit after December 1972’s Apollo 17. It is also the Space Launch System’s (SLS) second flight.Four NASA astronauts are carrying out the space mission:Reid Wiseman (Commander) – Former US Navy captain and test pilotVictor Glover – Naval officer and test pilotChristina Koch – EngineerJeremy Hansen – Royal Canadian Air Force colonel, aquanaut, and CSA astronautThe Artemis II has currently passed the equidistance point between the Earth and moon. You can check out the livestream on NASA’s official YouTube channel.Netflix and NASA inked a deal in Summer 2025, resulting in NASA+’s arrival on the OTT platform. However, since then, only a single livestream from July 31, 2025, has made it to the platform.Originally reported by Abdul Azim Naushad on ComingSoon.The post Netflix To Live Stream Artemis II Lunar Flyby, Global Release Time Revealed appeared first on Mandatory.",
